{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778602128446,"sessionID":"ses_1e31469a3ffeep6OOfqc8i3XXk","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-ae0abc8c2c96d57e","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"fibrocartilage"},"output":"Found 51 matches\n/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/__issue_context__.json:\n  Line 2:   \"body\": \"Please check that the term does not already exist by using the ontology search tool OLS:\\nhttps://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/ontologies/cl\\n\\n\\n**Preferred term label**\\nfibrochondrocyte progenitor cell \\n\\n**Synonyms** (add reference(s), please)\\nFCP- related synonym - abbreviation - PMID: [31871141](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31871141/)\\n\\n**Definition** (free text, with reference(s), please. PubMed ID format is PMID:XXXXXX)\\nA mesenchymal progenitor cell located in fibrocartilaginous tissues, along the fibrochondrocytic differentiation pathway that co-expresses both fibrochondrocyte markers (COL1A1, COL3A1) and mesenchymal stem cell markers (MCAM/CD146, MYLK) in humans. FCP demonstrates colony-forming capacity and multi-lineage differentiation potential toward osteogenic and adipogenic lineages. This cell serves as a progenitor for mature fibrochondrocytes and other meniscal cell types, with differentiation regulated by TGF-β signaling, focal adhesion, and extracellular matrix-receptor interaction pathways.\\n\\nPMID: [31871141](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31871141/)\\nPMID: [36338137](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/36338137/)\\n\\n**Parent cell type term** (check the hierarchy here https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/ontologies/cl)\\n\\nMesenchymal cell\\nProgenitor cell \\n\\n\\n**Anatomical structure where the cell type is found** (check Uberon for anatomical structures: https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/ontologies/uberon)\\n\\nPart of some ‘ fibrocartilage’\\nexpresses some 'cell surface glycoprotein MUC18'\\nexpresses some 'myosin light chain kinase, smooth muscle'\\nexpresses some 'collagen alpha-1(I) chain'\\nexpresses some 'collagen alpha-1(III) chain'\\n\\n\\n\\n**Your ORCID**\\nhttps://orcid.org/0009-0000-8480-9277\\n\\n**Additional notes or concerns**\\nI will add a link to fibrochondrocyte - 'develops from' some 'fibrochondrocyte progenitor cell' once the term is added\\n\",\n\n\n/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/__pr_result__/src/ontology/reports/summary_release.md:\n  Line 1795: | UBERON:0035847 | fibrocartilage enthesis                                          | has developmental contribution from            | CL:0000058 | chondroblast                                                                              |\n\n  Line 1796: | UBERON:0035847 | fibrocartilage enthesis                                          | has developmental contribution from            | CL:0000134 | mesenchymal stem cell                                                                     |\n\n  Line 1797: | UBERON:0035847 | fibrocartilage enthesis                                          | has developmental contribution from            | CL:0007001 | skeletogenic cell                                                                         |\n\n  Line 1798: | UBERON:0035847 | fibrocartilage enthesis                                          | has developmental contribution from            | CL:0007009 | prechondroblast                                                                           |\n\n\n/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/__pr_result__/src/ontology/imports/merged_import.owl:\n  Line 172538: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> \"ISBN:0073040584\") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> \"Wikipedia:Intervertebral_disk\") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001066> \"A pad of fibrocartilage between the articular surfaces of two successive vertebral centra which has nucleus pulposus at its core.\")\n\n  Line